1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:03,940
Fire maps say Earth burns six times more than twenty years ago.

2
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:07,740
It doesn't. New satellites simply see smaller fires.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,250
We're Team ALAZ, and this is ALAZ Relay.

4
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:15,820
From half a billion NASA fire detections, we taught VIIRS to count like MODIS:

5
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:19,310
one consistent record, that finds real disasters on its own.

6
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:23,010
Draw any place on Earth, and get its fire calendar since 2000.

7
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:25,750
When MODIS retires, the relay carries on.

8
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:28,750
Satellites changed. Fires didn't.
